00:40:50.939 --> 00:40:53.100
And as he was talking shit, hitting me,

00:40:53.100 --> 00:40:53.940
I remember telling him,

00:40:53.940 --> 00:40:55.950
just read your paper like
you do every morning.

00:40:55.950 --> 00:40:56.816
Because he was telling me,

00:40:56.816 --> 00:40:57.649
what are you gonna do about it,

00:40:57.649 --> 00:40:58.482
what are you gonna do about it?

00:40:58.482 --> 00:41:00.549
I told him just read
the paper every morning.

00:41:00.549 --> 00:41:02.107
Well, about a month later,

00:41:02.107 --> 00:41:04.810
I remember my grandma gets him his paper,

00:41:04.810 --> 00:41:06.010
handed the paper, now mind you,

00:41:06.010 --> 00:41:07.140
I've been home for like three days,

00:41:07.140 --> 00:41:08.880
I ain't went nowhere.

00:41:08.880 --> 00:41:10.620
So, he gets his paper,

00:41:10.620 --> 00:41:12.875
he looking, he's reading it,

00:41:12.875 --> 00:41:15.070
and I remember he stops,

00:41:15.070 --> 00:41:16.820
he looks up at me,

00:41:16.820 --> 00:41:17.800
he looks down at his paper,

00:41:17.800 --> 00:41:22.560
he drops his paper and he
never talked to me again, ever.

00:41:22.560 --> 00:41:24.037
And my grandfather raised me

00:41:24.037 --> 00:41:25.440
and my little brother, you know,

00:41:25.440 --> 00:41:27.430
he just never spoke with me ever.

00:41:27.430 --> 00:41:28.459
When I went to prison and in court,

00:41:28.459 --> 00:41:30.340
he went to every court date,

00:41:30.340 --> 00:41:31.450
but he never spoke with me,

00:41:31.450 --> 00:41:32.766
he never spoke to me, not a word.

00:41:32.766 --> 00:41:34.960
I guess, my grandfather was upset

00:41:34.960 --> 00:41:36.339
because he actually felt that

00:41:36.339 --> 00:41:40.180
I was the one that wasn't
out there hurting people,

00:41:40.180 --> 00:41:42.220
shooting people, but little did he know,

00:41:42.220 --> 00:41:43.210
I was the main one.

00:41:43.210 --> 00:41:44.739
But when he found out,

00:41:44.739 --> 00:41:47.566
he blamed himself because
he remembers the day

00:41:47.566 --> 00:41:49.040
that he took me and showed me

00:41:49.040 --> 00:41:50.170
the bullet holes in his house

00:41:50.170 --> 00:41:52.306
and told me that I wasn't
doing shit about it.

00:41:52.306 --> 00:41:54.560
So when he read his paper
and he looked at me,

00:41:54.560 --> 00:41:56.030
he put two and two together

00:41:56.030 --> 00:41:58.203
and my grandmother told me after years

00:41:58.203 --> 00:41:59.460
that he was acting like that,

00:41:59.460 --> 00:42:00.293
that the reason he talked to me

00:42:00.293 --> 00:42:02.058
because he felt that it was his fault

00:42:02.058 --> 00:42:04.870
that I ended up the way I ended up,

00:42:04.870 --> 00:42:06.360
because I was sent in prison and he felt

00:42:06.360 --> 00:42:07.370
that it was his fault.

00:42:07.370 --> 00:42:08.543
Which it wasn't his fault at all,

00:42:08.543 --> 00:42:09.938
I was gonna go back anyways,

00:42:09.938 --> 00:42:11.000
that was my thing.

00:42:11.000 --> 00:42:11.870
We're gonna go back and forth,

00:42:11.870 --> 00:42:13.610
back and forth till one of
us can't go back no more.

00:42:13.610 --> 00:42:15.237
But the thing about it was is that

00:42:15.237 --> 00:42:17.273
now I had to remember these
two shootings in my house

00:42:17.273 --> 00:42:19.490
with 3030 and it's going
through every wall,

00:42:19.490 --> 00:42:21.260
so he's out to get somebody,

00:42:21.260 --> 00:42:23.230
so I ended up getting this dude,

00:42:23.230 --> 00:42:24.540
putting him the hospital

00:42:24.540 --> 00:42:25.830
and he never came back again.

00:42:25.830 --> 00:42:27.778
I think, I seen him
previous like 10 years ago

00:42:27.778 --> 00:42:29.900
and he walks all messed up,

00:42:29.900 --> 00:42:30.733
you know what I mean?

00:42:30.733 --> 00:42:32.260
He got shot really, really bad.

00:42:32.260 --> 00:42:34.640
You know, he was the one that
I made pop lock on the floor.

00:42:34.640 --> 00:42:36.030
What I mean by pop lock is,

00:42:36.030 --> 00:42:38.809
I had a .22 rifle that sure shot 38 rounds

00:42:38.809 --> 00:42:40.630
and there were 22 bullets.

00:42:40.630 --> 00:42:42.669
And they way, when you hit somebody,

00:42:42.669 --> 00:42:44.360
you hit them so much that

00:42:44.360 --> 00:42:45.901
they actually look like
they're pop locking

00:42:45.901 --> 00:42:47.671
because you're just shaking
everywhere, you know.

00:42:47.671 --> 00:42:49.900
And I say, let's go make us some pop lock,

00:42:49.900 --> 00:42:52.690
and I used to let whole the clip up

00:42:52.690 --> 00:42:54.177
and watch a guy pop lock, you know.

00:42:54.177 --> 00:42:55.320
Then when they hit the ground,

00:42:55.320 --> 00:42:56.153
you hit them on the ground,

00:42:56.153 --> 00:42:57.660
now their break dancing because
they spinning, you know.

00:42:57.660 --> 00:42:58.980
A lot of people would spin, you know

00:42:58.980 --> 00:43:00.520
so we were clown like that and say,

00:43:00.520 --> 00:43:02.457
hey let's go make somebody pop lock.

00:43:02.457 --> 00:43:04.188
And I remember I had their .22 rifle,

00:43:04.188 --> 00:43:06.020
I sawed the front of it off

